<activity xml:id="act-GraphRefresher">
    <title>A Refresher on Graphing Functions</title>
    <introduction>
        <p>
            This is, again, mostly a discussion activity. There's not much to <em>do</em>, but you should think about these questions and share your thoughts with others.
        </p>
    </introduction>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                How do we plot a typical function (in the form <m>y=f(x)</m>) on a coordinate grid? How do you think about the different variables, and how do we use them to plot a point?
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                How do we represent the coordinates of a point? What does each component of a point tell us about its location?
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Does the <q>grid</q> that we use match with the way you might think about locations of things in your life? Where else do humans use a grid like this to describe locations?
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
</activity>